Z||000000||varnster||03-16-2001||10:32 AM||||I just replaced my ignition switch and got<BR>turn signal and hazard switch reconnected,<BR>my problem is the spring that is on the steering shaft(that the wheel bolts to)HAS<BR>SPRUNG. and I cant get the black cover back<BR>on I can push it in but the spring pressure is so great their is no way I can put the little snap ring on while pushing in on the black cover.when I first took of the black<BR>cover their was no spring pressure, this makes me think im doing something wrong I<BR>cant find any info on this, PLEASE HELP A <BR>BROTHER OUT! ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-16-2001||06:42 PM||||You was lucky...<BR>You need a tool to compress the spring...<BR>NAPA has em...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by varnster:<BR><B>I just replaced my ignition switch and got<BR>turn signal and hazard switch reconnected,<BR>my problem is the spring that is on the steering shaft(that the wheel bolts to)HAS<BR>SPRUNG. and I cant get the black cover back<BR>on I can push it in but the spring pressure is so great their is no way I can put the little snap ring on while pushing in on the black cover.when I first took of the black<BR>cover their was no spring pressure, this makes me think im doing something wrong I<BR>cant find any info on this, PLEASE HELP A <BR>BROTHER OUT! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-16-2001||07:43 PM||||Assembly order.... Spring, metal plate, snap ring, plastic cover. You likely need the tool to get the ring back on as well as off. I usually do. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||03-16-2001||09:18 PM||||I think the tool you are looking for is called a lock plate depressor.  Should be availabel at any auto parts store.  Often you can borrow one by leaving a deposit until it is returned.  AutoZone does this.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
